$+comments
MICROSEMI ZL88602 Multiline Inverting Boost 8 FXS %0D%0ADec 9, 2016 JLR%0D%0A%0D%0AThis profile defines the switcher parameters for the 8FXS design.%0D%0AIn this design Device one switcher Y is the master for the VBL supply%0D%0Abut switcher Z is a slave.  Device 2 swicher Z is the master for the%0D%0AVBH supply and switcher Y is a slave.  The control of the VBL and VBH%0D%0Aswitchers are spread across two devices.  This is to minimize loading%0D%0Aon each devices VDDSW supply which is powered from an internal%0D%0Acharge pump. %0D%0A%0D%0ADevice profiles also include softstart timing parameters.%0D%0AThis loads limited switcher timing for a specified period (50ms in this case)%0D%0Ato limit inrush current during start up. This can be modified if startup%0D%0Acurrent is too high.%0D%0A%0D%0AVBAT supplies are configured as follows:%0D%0A%0D%0AVBL device 1 SWY(master)- 25V, FSW= 300kHz, VDDSW=4.7V (device mode reg)%0D%0A             SWZ(slave) - 76V%0D%0A  I/O21_VS1 Analog- Open%0D%0A  I/O22_VS2 Analog - VSW sense%0D%0A  Softstart Enabled - 50ms%0D%0A  Overcurrent shutdown sense on VS1%0D%0A%0D%0AVBH device 2 SWY (slave) - 25V%0D%0A             SWZ (master) - 76V, Fsw 192kHz, VDDSW=5V (device mode reg)%0D%0A  I/O21_VS1 Analog - Open%0D%0A  I/O22_VS2 Digital - uncommitted %0D%0A  Softstart Enabled - 50ms %0D%0A  Overcurrent shutdown sense on VS1%0D%0A%0D%0AAll other devices: SWY (slave) - 25V%0D%0A                   SWZ (slave) - 76V%0D%0A  All I/Os digital and uncommitted%0D%0A%0D%0A%0D%0ADevice 1 I/O22_VS2 can be used to measure the VSW input supply.  This may%0D%0Abe important to support wide input supply voltages where alternate switcher%0D%0Aprofiles may need to be loaded.
